# CG

Display name is **CG** (broadcast Character Generator). Keep it. Do **not** rename to Overlay, Graphics, GFX, Live, Board, or Item.

This is the locked vocabulary for code, UI copy, DB, routes, and the subdomain. If a new Element needs a payload key, add it under `payload` jsonb — do not invent a parallel table or a second token scheme.

| Surface | Locked name |
|---|---|
| Launcher / `tyapp_app_feature.name` | `CG` |
| Route | `/cg` (`/cg/list`, `/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/:id`, `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId`) |
| Overlay path | `/o/:token` on the CG host; fallback `/cg-live/:token` on Jaxfr |
| Subdomain | `cg` → `https://cg.tszyin.com` / `http://cg.localhost:4200` |
| Code | `features/cg/`, `apps/cg/` (overlay), `core/domains/cg/` |
| Panel files | `cg-package-edit.*` (skeleton is `*-edit`; the page is still Panel) |
| Layer desk | `cg-layer-edit.*` nested on the Panel at `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId` (same right column as tiles — not a second page) |

## UI words

| Word | Means | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Package** | One look to use together | CH36, News SNG |
| **Element** | Kind in the catalog (code registry `CG_ELEMENT_CATALOG`) | Logo, Clock, Ticker |
| **Layer** | One instance inside a Package | CH36's Logo |
| **Panel** | This Package's operator page | Left Package (main), right Layers |
| **Output** | OBS URL (full-frame transparent Stage) | Package Output (default), Layer Output |
| **Stage** | 16:9 canvas | Tile thumbs, On air / Pending, overlay |
| **On air** | What OBS has (last Save, or live in Direct) | Monitor(s) in the left column |
| **Pending** | Unsaved draft mix (**Studio mode** only) | Save promotes it to On air |
| **Direct** | OBS-style: edit Program live | One On air monitor; auto-save to air |
| **Studio mode** | OBS Studio Mode: Preview then Program | Pending \| On air; Save to air |

**Channel / Source** stay on the Package as `role`. Clock is not Timer. Overlay is the public page implementation, not a product noun. Welcome → CG and every CG subpage (list / Panel) skip the Jaxfr page crossfade — instant swap, no 200ms fade. Other Jaxfr features keep the Aero transition. UI copy is **sentence case** (no `text-transform: uppercase` kickers/buttons). **Studio mode** (edit) is not the **Alpha / Dim** stage backdrop.

**Panel layout:** one page, two columns — **Package** (master surface, card bg + soft depth) vs **Layers** (nested workbench, quieter bg). Prefer spacing / surface over hairline borders so it does not read as six peer boxes. Header: Back + Package + Alpha/Dim + Copy OBS; Layers header: Layers + Alpha/Dim + catalog. Monitor section, then Name / Role / Appear / Look, then footer Delete package (`mat-flat-button.danger-btn`, dark red + white). Right: tiles then selected Layer desk as one inset card (settings | visual). Desk footer: Delete layer + Copy layer OBS. Click selected tile again to close desk. Package title is heavier than Layers.

**Edit mode (per package, localStorage `cg-package-edit-mode:{id}`):**
- **Studio mode** ON (default): two monitors Pending \| On air on the **Package** column. Package mix waits for **Take**: name, role, Appear, Package Look, Layer existence / On-Off / z-order. **Logo Layer content** defaults to Direct (Live) even while Package Studio is on — see Logo desk Studio below. Subtitle cue stays the live path it already was.
- **Studio mode** OFF (= Direct): Package column one On air monitor. Package mix also auto-saves (debounced) + Realtime broadcast. **Take** hidden once the package exists (first **Create** still needed). Turning Studio mode off with unsaved dirty promotes immediately.
- Workflow to hide mid-edit from air: Package Off → **Take** → edit Layer (live but Off) → On → **Take**. Skipping Take after Off means layout edits can still hit OBS while visible — accepted risk; watch Package **On air** (right).

**Logo desk Studio mode (per Logo layer, localStorage `cg-layer-studio:{layerId}`, default OFF = Live):**
- Separate from Package Studio. **No second monitor** — desk Stage always shows what you are editing.
- **When layer is on air (`layer.visible === true` in package):** every change goes live instantly — Studio mode switch is disabled and forced OFF (Live mode).
- **When layer is not on air (`layer.visible === false` in package):** operator can toggle Studio mode ON or OFF:
  - **OFF (Live):** Name / Look / Source / Place write through to DB + On air / OBS (debounced).
  - **ON (Draft):** edits stay local to desk monitor until **Apply** (promote to On air + DB) or **Discard** (restore last Apply). Top-right Layer Items Bar (`cg-drive` tiles) reflects what is committed / on-air (`tileLayer(layer)`), so tiles do not update until Apply or Save.
- Turning Studio off with dirty discards or promotes. Subtitle desk has no Studio switch (always Live).

**Controls & heights on Panel & Desk:**
- All control buttons (`.cg-seg-btn`), segmented toggle groups (`.cg-seg-toggle`), and textboxes / selects (`input`, `select`) share a uniform **28px outer height** (`box-sizing: border-box`).
- Inputs & selects use `1px` border with `box-sizing: border-box; height: 28px;` so their total outer height matches buttons exactly.
- Segmented toggle groups use `height: 28px; box-sizing: border-box;` with inner button overrides `height: 26px` (accounting for the 2px top/bottom border).
- Action buttons (`.cg-seg-btn`) strictly enforce `height: 28px; min-height: 28px; max-height: 28px; line-height: 28px; box-sizing: border-box;` overriding Aero's `32px` global button style.
- On Layer desk, `.cg-monitor-toolbar` is locked to `28px` (`height: 28px; min-height: 28px; max-height: 28px; box-sizing: border-box; flex-shrink: 0; overflow: hidden;`) so the preview monitor stays at the exact same vertical position whether Studio mode is toggled ON or OFF (with or without Apply / Discard buttons).

**Always desktop on Panel only:** Panel (`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…`) locks the viewport to `width=1280` and `min-width: 1280px`. Phone and tablet keep the same 3-pane (pinch-zoom / horizontal pan) — do not add a stacked `@media` reflow. **List** uses normal responsive width like Attendance. Overlay `/o` and `/cg-live` stay `width=device-width`. Unlock the viewport when leaving Panel.

**No fixed palette — CG follows the operator's own Aero/Material + light/dark choice:** an earlier pass gave CG admin a fixed "broadcast console" identity (`_cg-theme.scss`); that was reverted (2026-09-24) after live review — the user wants the traditional skeuomorphic 3D "Windows 7 Aero / iOS 6" button look for themselves, but their partner prefers flat Material, and the app's existing per-user `visual_theme`/`color_mode` toggle (`UserPreferenceService`/`ThemeService`) already resolves that tension app-wide. CG does not need — and must not reintroduce — a third, fixed identity. `_cg-theme.scss` and its `console-light`/`console-dark` mixins are deleted; do not recreate them.

**Buttons are real Angular Material components, not hand-rolled `<button class="cg-btn">`:** either-choice groups (Channel/Source, Fade/Cut, Color/B&W, Alpha/Dim, News/Show, Cue Fade/Cut) use `mat-button-toggle-group.cg-seg-toggle` — same merged chrome as App Log's version bump toggle. One-shot actions (Delete / Copy OBS `content_copy` / Choose local image / catalog / cue / Copy) use `mat-stroked-button.cg-seg-btn`. Only **Create** / **Take** / Logo **Apply** stay `mat-flat-button` primary. **Studio mode** is a labeled `.cg-switch` in the Package monitor toolbar and again on the Logo desk (content Draft). Sentence case labels — no uppercase transform. Aero/Material look comes from `_aero-controls.scss` plus the toggle overrides. Layer `.cg-switch` On/Off stays as before. Back is a plain circular `<a class="cg-back">`. Header Alpha/Dim sit next to Package / Layers titles as the same text toggle (not icon glyphs); Package Copy OBS (`content_copy`) sits immediately after Package Alpha/Dim; Layers catalog is `margin-left: auto` so chips trail right. Destructive actions use app-wide `mat-flat-button.danger-btn` (dark red fill, white label — see `_tokens` / `_aero-controls`).

**No global toolbar:** `<app-toolbar>` is hidden for CG **Panel** paths (`/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/…`) via `isCgPanelPath()`. **List** (`/cg`, `/cg/list`) uses the normal AppToolbar through `HeaderService` — same pattern as Attendance (title, back to Welcome, Refresh, New package). Panel keeps Back / Studio mode / Take inline.

## Tables and columns (final)

`tyapp_cg_package` PK `tb_tyapp_cgpk_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgpk_seq_no`):

`name`, `role` (`channel` \| `source`), `public_token`, `duration_ms` (`0` = cut, default `400` = fade), `look` (`color` \| `mono`), `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

`tyapp_cg_layer` PK `tb_tyapp_cgly_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgly_seq_no`):

`package_id` → package PK, `element_type`, `public_token`, `layout` jsonb, `payload` jsonb, `visible` (On/Off), `look` (`inherit` \| `color` \| `mono`; default `inherit` = Package Look), `sort_order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

Layout jsonb: `x`, `y`, `unit` (`percent` \| `px`), `anchor`, `scale`, `width`, `height`. **Logo Place** is inset-from-anchor: X/Y are offsets from the Anchor edges (Top right + 5,5 = 5 from the right and top). Logo desk UI exposes Anchor as a 3x3 directional button grid (`cg-anchor-toggle-group`) with arrow icons (dark blue when selected), and X / Y / Scale inputs with wheel adjustment (no Unit / Width controls); optional stored `width` still applies if present. Logo `scale` is a CSS transform. Desk **Outline** toggle (not saved, not OBS) draws a thick yellow rim + red outer shadow for placement. **Subtitle** still uses point-in-frame (x/y = where the Anchor sits on Stage). Subtitle `scale` only multiplies type size (`1` = ffmpeg FontSize 16.1 / PlayRes 288, about 5.6% of frame height); Show preset Scale 1 is about 7.2% of frame height. The caption stays inside `width` and wraps. Overlay uses `vh` so Browser Source gets on-air size even when `cqh` does not. News look is white fill, regular weight, `ScaleY` 1.11, `Spacing` 1.68. Black outline is a **behind** `-webkit-text-stroke` copy (fill sits on top). Do not put stroke and fill on the same span — OBS CEF has no `paint-order`, and 8-way `text-shadow` makes a jagged octagon around CJK. Show is larger, slightly gold, thicker behind-stroke. Latin runs use Segoe UI / Arial; CJK stays 華康中黑體 / JhengHei.

Logo payload jsonb: `imageUrl` (http(s) or app path such as `/icons/3d/apps.png` — **never** a `data:image` base64 string), `fileName`. "Choose local image" uploads PNG/WebP to the public Storage bucket `cg-logo` (`CgService.uploadLogoImage`) and stores only the public URL. Overlay used to poll `tyapp_cg_get_output_by_token` every 300ms forever; embedding the file in `payload` re-transmitted it on every poll (uncached PostgREST egress). Overlay now subscribes to Realtime broadcast `cg-output:{token}` (Panel sends on Save / live cue) and only hits that RPC on connect plus a 30s safety poll. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-logo-storage.sql`. Do not drop `tyapp_cg_*` tables for this.

Subtitle payload jsonb: `lines` (string[]), `index` (`number` \| `null` = blank / off air), `cursor` (last clicked row; kept when Blank), `style.preset` (`news` \| `show`; default `news`), `transition.duration_ms` (cue crossfade; `0` = cut, default `400`). This is **not** Package Appear.

Tokens share one `/o/:token` space (unique across both tables in practice). Do not add a token table.

RPCs: `tyapp_cg_package_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_layer_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_get_output_by_token`.

**Save** (Studio mode) writes the Package and applies it to Output. **Direct** auto-saves the same payload on each change (quiet toast). Each Layer **fades in or out on its own** using the Package `duration_ms` (`0` = cut). Layers that did not change stay put — turning Weather On does not blink an already-On Logo. Panel tile order is Stage **z-order** (first tile behind, last in front); drag to reorder, then Save (Studio) or auto-save (Direct).

**Host vs inner:** Package / Panel owns mix — which Layers exist, On/Off, z-order, OBS URL, **Appear** (Fade / Cut + `duration_ms` for the whole Layer going on or off), and **Package Look** as a master bus. Package B&W greys **every** Layer (Layer Color cannot punch out). Package Color lets a Layer set Color / B&W. Layer desk does **not** have its own Appear. Cue crossfade, News / Show, layout, and later inner animation live on the Layer (`payload.transition.duration_ms` for cue). Package Cut must not force cue to cut.

**Ownership (locked):** Package Studio gates **mix only** (membership, On/Off, z-order, Package Look, Appear). **Layer content** never waits for Package Take and never marks Package Unsaved. Default for Logo is Live Direct; optional Logo Studio Draft gates Name / Look / Source / Place until Apply. Subtitle cue / layout / Look / Style stay Live. Workflow to edit off-air: Package Off → Take → edit Layer (desk still shows it via `forceVisible`; Package monitors hide it) → On → Take. Take/Create flushes pending Layer Live writes then updates mix columns only on existing layer rows (new rows still full-insert on first Create).

**Save scope:**
- **Studio mode:** **Take** applies name, role, Appear, Package Look, and every Layer's existence / On-Off / z-order — not Layer content. Logo Live + subtitle cue write through without Take; Logo Draft waits for Apply.
- **Direct:** Package mix fields auto-save (debounced ~450ms). Layer content still uses its own Live / Draft path (independent of Package mode).

**On air / Pending:**
- **Studio mode:** two small 16:9 Stages — **Pending left**, **On air right**. On air mix = last Take (OBS On/Off / z-order / Package fields). Layer **content** on On air updates live when Logo is Live (or after Apply in Draft). Pending = draft mix (+ desk draft content when editing). New unsaved Package: On air empty.
- **Direct:** one On air Stage (draft === air for mix). Auto-save + broadcast on change. Logo Draft still holds content off OBS until Apply.
- Live cue (Up / Down / Blank / Paste / Load) **and Cue Fade / Cut** always update On air immediately in both modes. Alpha / Dim stage toggles sit next to **Package** (left monitors) and **Layers** (tiles + Layer desk) — no Backdrop label.

**Layer desk monitors:** always a **single** preview for that one Layer (Logo Studio Draft does not add a second monitor). Own local Alpha/Dim backdrop; does not replace Package monitors. Desk Look is **Layer Look only** (`layerLookOnly`) — Package B&W does **not** grey the desk; tiles / Package monitors / OBS still use Package Look as master bus. Desk preview **force-shows** the layer even when Package On/Off is Off (`forceVisible`) — same idea as tile thumbs — so you can still place/style while it's hidden from the mix / OBS. Desk does not bind Package Appear duration.

**Logo / Layer desk shell:** Tiles = chrome on top (`drag_indicator` + z + On/Off), Stage thumb in the middle, **name** on the bottom (custom `name`, or Element type if blank). Desk splits left/right: left = Logo **Studio mode** switch (+ Apply / Discard when on) + Stage ~450px + **Name | Look** (same `cg-block-title` style, side by side) + **Source** (Logo) + **Copy to package** + footer Delete layer via `danger-btn` + Copy layer OBS; right = **Place** for Logo — Anchor / X / Y / Scale + Outline switch (or Cue / Style for Subtitle). Place number fields accept scroll-wheel adjust (hover, no focus required). Place inputs use fixed reasonable width (not full column). Layers column header holds Alpha/Dim for tiles + desk. Package Look master bus greys tiles + Package monitors + OBS; desk editing monitor stays independent. No Inherit / Follow package. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-layer-name.sql`.

Greyscale is a per-layer host `filter` and always **cuts** (no fade) — Package Appear only drives host opacity On/Off on mix/OBS. It must not change z-order.

**Subtitle cue is the live exception:** Up / Down / click / Paste / Load .txt or .srt patches only `lines` / `index` / `cursor` immediately (no Package Save). Cue bar uses `keyboard_arrow_up` / `keyboard_arrow_down` / `content_paste` icons; **Blank** and **Load .txt / .srt** stay words. Cue Fade / Cut patches `payload.transition.duration_ms` the same way (`0` = cut, default `400`) — it is **not** Package Appear, and it does **not** wait for Save. Unsaved News/Show must not leak to OBS. Overlay gets cue via Realtime broadcast (plus a 30s RPC safety poll) and shows `lines[index]`. Cue changes **crossfade** with that Layer duration; this is inside the caption, not Layer On/Off opacity. `index = null` is blank air; `cursor` stays on the last clicked row so Down continues from there and Up puts it back. SRT import strips sequence numbers and timestamps; each cue becomes one queue line. Subtitle desk shows Cue Fade/Cut next to Up / Down / Blank, then Scale / Y / Width (bottom-center, `%`), plus News / Show. Logo still has full X/Y/Width/Scale/Anchor/Unit.

**Copy Layer** INSERTs a new row into another Package: new PK, new `public_token` (never share the OBS URL), `index = null`. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-layer-look.sql`.

Do not revive `tyapp_cg_slot` or `component_type`.
